course: dictionary
lesson: 15928
title: The word unread
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix un- often means not, and read means to look at words and understand them. So unread means not read yet. «The book on my desk is still unread.» I have not opened it.
explain: Unread can describe things you could read, such as a book, a page or a message. «Mum has twelve unread messages on her phone.» Each message is waiting, and nobody has looked at it yet.
explain: In maths, unread can mean the part you have not read yet. «The story has 200 pages and I have read 120, so 80 pages are unread.» To find the unread pages, take the pages you have read away from the total: 200 - 120 = 80.
fact: Unread means not read yet.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in unhappy, unkind and unread.
fact: An unread book or message is one that nobody has read.
fact: In maths, the unread pages are the total pages minus the pages already read.
fact: Unread can also describe a person who has not read much, but this use is rare.
exercise: «Mum has twelve unread messages on her phone.» What does unread mean here? | *Not read yet | Deleted for good | Read out loud to everyone | Sent to the wrong person
exercise: «The story has 200 pages and I have read 120, so 80 pages are unread.» How many pages are unread? | *80 | 320 | 200 | 120
exercise: «The unread letters sat in a pile by the door.» Find and copy the word that means not read yet. | pile | *unread | door | letters
test: «Dad left the newspaper unread on the table.» Which word tells you the newspaper was not read? | *Unread | Dad | Newspaper | Table
test: A school has 60 library books and 45 have been read. How many library books are unread? | *15 | 45 | 60 | 105
exam: Which sentence uses unread correctly? | I read the book, so it is unread now | Unread is what I did to the story yesterday | *The message is unread, because nobody has opened it yet | The unread cake was eaten by everyone at lunch
